<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-subspaces" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Subspaces, Basis, and Dimension</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Lines and planes through the origin, spans, and the sets of vectors a matrix sends
      to zero all share a common structure: they are closed under linear combinations.
      This chapter isolates that structure, shows that every such set is a span of
      linearly independent vectors, and attaches a single number <mdash /> the
      dimension <mdash /> to each one.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="subspaces/sec-subspaces.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="subspaces/sec-basis-dimension.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="subspaces/sec-column-null-space.ptx" />

</chapter>
